Vikram and Betal: The Careful Speaker (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100144

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a man who spoke without thinking,” said Betal. “He often hurt others with his words.”

One day, he said something unkind to his friend.

His friend felt very sad.

Later, the man realized his mistake and said sorry.

But his friend replied, “Your words hurt me deeply.”

The man went to a wise elder for advice.

The elder gave him a bag of feathers and said, “Drop these feathers around the village.”

The man did as he was told.

Then the elder said, “Now collect all the feathers.”

The man said, “That is impossible! They have blown away.”

The elder smiled and said, “Words are like feathers. Once spoken, they cannot be taken back.”

The man understood his mistake and learned to speak carefully.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what is the lesson here?”

Vikram replied, “We should think before we speak.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Think before you speak.
